{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC segmenting Markdown to wiki renderer\n\n## Problem and boundaries\nDC stores wiki markup while rebar authors Markdown and currently sends Markdown literally. Whole-body pandoc 3.6.1 escapes prose/code arrows, erodes tables, and deletes `<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->`.\n\nAdd an unwired pure renderer. `WikiTextCodec.fit_outbound` retains 32,767-character truncation; `normalize_outbound`/`to_wire` stay identity; `decode_inbound` stays identity plus None-to-empty. `OutboundFieldMapper`, CREATE, `normalize_rich_text`, and live sends stay unchanged. Story 3388 owns cutover, echo suppression, and codec-law convergence. Story 5c0e owns timeout/process/GPL/SBOM hardening. Cloud uses its ADF child.\n\nPandoc's maintained CommonMark/Jira pair produced 98.4% eligible-character coverage; surveyed md-to-jira, mistune-jira, and md-jira lack equivalent maintained fidelity. Selective segmentation contains damage. ADR 0083 governs imports. ADR 0095 plus its `.numbers/0095` marker records invariants, empirical pin provenance, alternatives, platform boundary, and deferrals.\n\n## Corpus\nCommit a deterministic, fixed-seed scrubbed sample from `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py`: 29 code-arrow, 29 table, and 120 prose bodies (178); shards stay below 500 KB. Records declare source, protected excerpts, and eligible units independently of output. Exclude the fixture from criteria vocabulary; reject emails, tenant hostnames, and URLs.\n\nEligible means a classifier-6 unit dispatched to pandoc. Body ratio = bodies with a changed eligible unit / 178; character ratio = source characters in changed eligible units / all eligible-unit source characters. Pin measured 0.927/0.984; require >=0.90/>=0.95 and changed outputs.\n\n## Renderer contract\nAdd `adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` with `render_markdown_to_wiki(markdown: str) -> str`.\n\nTwo-phase left-to-right lexer:\n1. Lock complete `{noformat}` spans, backtick/tilde fences, and four-space-indented blocks, including internal blank lines.\n2. Split intervening text into blank-line blocks plus list items; preserve separators/order.\n\nClassify, in order:\n1. Locked blocks and units beginning `h1.`-`h6.`, `{code}`, or `{noformat}` pass exactly.\n2. An inline-Jira scanner masks code, then recognizes balanced nonempty `*strong*` (single markers, never `**`), `_emphasis_`, `[label|target]`, `{color:name}...{color}`, and `{{monospace}}`. Pass exactly only with a recognized span, all significant delimiters consumed, and no CommonMark-only heading/quote/list/fence/backtick/`**`/image/`[label](target)`. Malformed or mixed markup continues. Ambiguous isolated `*text*`/`_text_` favors preservation; ADR records the false-positive tradeoff.\n3. ASCII table = >=2 pipe-bearing lines with a pipes/colons/hyphens/whitespace delimiter row. Wrap exact bytes once in `{noformat}`.\n4. HTML comment or tag matching `<[/!]?[A-Za-z][^>]*>` passes exactly.\n5. Prose outside extracted code containing `(?`, `\\b`, `\\d`, `\\s`, `\\w`, or a bracket class followed by `*`, `+`, `?`, or `{n,m}` passes exactly.\n6. Remaining headings, quotes, list items, and prose render via pypandoc `commonmark -> jira` with `--wrap=none`.\n\nCode fragments are fences, four-space blocks, and inline spans with matching backtick runs. Mask them before classifiers and arrows. In renderable units make one regex pass ordered `<!--`, `-->`, `<->`, `->`, `<-`, `=>`; map arrows to ↔/→/←/⇒ and delimiters to themselves. Inline code copies exactly.\n\nEvery extracted fragment must appear byte-identically in order after conversion or that unit falls back. Strip content-free `{anchor:}` after headings. Five-pass tests start from Markdown, capture first-pass outputs containing Jira bold, italic, link, color, and monospace (real pandoc where supported; controlled successful converter output otherwise), then prove passes 2-5 byte-identical. Separate fixtures cover pre-existing wiki.\n\nMissing pypandoc returns the body and warns `wiki_render_fallback` with only `reason=\"pandoc_absent\"`. Conversion/preservation failure returns the unit and debugs the same event with only `reason=\"conversion_failure\"`/`\"preservation_failure\"`; never log bodies. Module state is immutable.\n\n## Dependency and CI\nAdd `wiki = [\"pypandoc-binary==1.15\"]` plus wiki in dev, register its pypandoc probe, and lock. Optionality adds `wiki:wiki`, removes `eval:eval`, and changes the union to `agents,tracing,wiki`. Dynamic tests `test_optionality_loop_covers_every_declared_extra` and `test_eval_extra_is_gone` plus full suite prove parity.\n\nAn exact-pin, non-skipping test hard-imports pypandoc, proves versions 1.15/3.6.1 and exact `commonmark -> jira` heading output (not `get_pandoc_formats`). It gates project Linux/macOS CI; Windows wheels are supported, while core/BSD identity fallback is a separate boundary. Wiki tests never importorskip.\n\nChanged paths: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py`; `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py`; `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py`; `pyproject.toml`; `uv.lock`; `src/rebar/_optional.py`; `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`; `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`; `docs/adr/0095-dc-segmenting-wiki-renderer.md`; `docs/adr/.numbers/0095`.\n\n## Verification and surfaces\nAuthor the full oracle RED-first; collect without skip/xfail. Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test`; prove resolution with `uv sync --locked --extra wiki --extra agents --extra tracing` under the same PATH. No contention test: stateless transform, no store composition, retry/backoff, or cache.\n\nCLI/MCP/API/public facade: out of scope because this is unwired. Automated callers plus dual direction: story 3388. Cloud: ADF child.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Classifier-6 units render through real pandoc in order; `test_dc_segmenting_passthrough`.\n- [ ] Tables preserve exact bytes once; table passthrough and five-pass tests.\n- [ ] HTML/regex-dangerous units preserve exact bytes; passthrough tests.\n- [ ] Specified arrows convert prose; `test_arrow_substitution_cases`.\n- [ ] Code arrows and prose/code `-->` stay exact; arrow tests.\n- [ ] 29 code-arrow fixtures retain protected excerpts; corpus test.\n- [ ] 29 tables keep exact bytes inside one noformat wrapper over five passes.\n- [ ] HTML comments survive exactly; corpus HTML test.\n- [ ] Block and inline Jira forms stay byte-identical for five passes.\n- [ ] Markdown-first bold/italic/link/color/monospace outputs stabilize after pass one.\n- [ ] Missing pandoc returns exact body and content-free `wiki_render_fallback:pandoc_absent`.\n- [ ] Conversion failure returns exact unit and logs only `conversion_failure`.\n- [ ] Preservation failure returns exact unit and logs only `preservation_failure`.\n- [ ] wiki locks pypandoc-binary 1.15; packaging test.\n- [ ] wiki installs alone and jointly without eval; uv sync and optionality lane.\n- [ ] Real binary is pandoc 3.6.1 and exact jira heading conversion succeeds.\n- [ ] Body ratio >=0.90 and character ratio >=0.95 over eligible source.\n- [ ] Cardinality is 29+29+120=178; pinned cardinality test.\n- [ ] Fixtures contain no email, tenant hostname, or URL; secrets test.\n- [ ] Heading output has no content-free anchor; passthrough test.\n- [ ] ADR marker passes `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`.\n- [ ] ADR has Decision/Invariants/Pin/Alternatives/Platform/Deferrals; ADR test.\n- [ ] Existing WikiTextCodec tests stay unmodified; full suite."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786573716026220001,"uuid":"4d1ddd49-b269-48c3-bc0f-fd6591fe1dd9"}